## 14. User-Facing Explanation Rules

Define how the assistant should explain language-related limitations or clarifications.

The assistant should explain language issues when:

* translation confidence is low
* a term may have multiple meanings
* the user’s wording affects routing or eligibility
* an official term must be preserved
* human review is needed due to language ambiguity

Preferred explanation patterns:

```text
I want to make sure I route this correctly. When you say “[term],” do you mean [option A] or [option B]?
```

```text
I’ll keep your original wording in the case record and also include a translated summary for review.
```

```text
This term may map to more than one service category, so I need one clarification before proceeding.
```

Avoid:

* blaming the user’s language
* saying the system “does not understand” when a more specific explanation is possible
* exposing internal classification logic unnecessarily
* over-explaining translation mechanics

